@startuml
title Balance, Expense Posting, and Payment Settlement (proposed)
left to right direction
rectangle "Approved expense" as Expense
rectangle "Payer credit\n+amount paid" as Credit
rectangle "Participant share debits\n- allocated shares" as Debits
rectangle "Authoritative ledger / transactional\nfinancial records (source of truth)" as Ledger
rectangle "Rebuildable balance projection\n(derived read model; may be stale)" as Balance
rectangle "Payment request" as Request
rectangle "Authenticate and authorize actor" as Auth
rectangle "Begin payment transaction" as Begin
rectangle "Read authoritative outstanding amount\ninside transaction" as ReadDue
rectangle "Check requested amount against\ncurrent outstanding amount" as Check
rectangle "Reject excess; return current\namount due; no financial effect" as Reject
rectangle "Commit payment and ledger effect\natomically; deduplicate request" as Payment
rectangle "Update or invalidate projection,\nthen commit transaction" as Commit
rectangle "Updated amount due" as Due
Expense --> Credit
Expense --> Debits
Credit --> Ledger
Debits --> Ledger
Ledger --> Balance : derive / rebuild
Request --> Auth
Auth --> Begin
Begin --> ReadDue
Ledger --> ReadDue
ReadDue --> Check
Check --> Reject : amount > current due
Check --> Payment : 0 < amount <= current due
Payment --> Ledger
Payment --> Commit
Commit --> Balance : update or invalidate
Commit --> Due
Balance --> Due : read only; not payment authority
note bottom
Payer may be a participant; their share offsets payer credit.
Pending/rejected expense has no ledger posting. Duplicate requests
cannot create duplicate effects. Concurrent payment control is required;
locking/isolation/version strategy depends on persistence technology.
No cross-currency arithmetic without approved conversion.
end note
@enduml
